    "done_when": "Root cause (run r-20261002T225511267666, merged 2bbec7a04, benchmarks/moment_map_derivative_contract.py): on the fixture of test_the_moment_map_is_differentiable_against_finite_differences, TopologyState.boundary_flux (nova/equilibrium/topology.py:1355, data_b = where(boundary_is_xpoint, data_x, data_w) after :1314, with data_x from polish_receipt['selected_value']) is the first stage whose central difference disagrees, at 0.394 for a 1e-5 step. Reverse mode and the JVP agree on it to 2.1e-14, and axis_flux agrees to 8.3e-10. Contract, from the locked decision separatrix-spline-extraction polish-termination (reverse mode from implicit differentiation at grad psi(x*) = 0, never through the polish loop): with the topology class and the selected boundary point held at the terminal state, d(boundary_flux) equals the flux perturbation evaluated at the admitted boundary point. At an X-point the position term vanishes because grad psi = 0 there. At a limiter contact the position moves along the wall, and the tangential term vanishes at the constrained extremum. First find which part of the current path breaks this, by file and line: polish value, interpolation stencil, wall-point selection, or a stop_gradient. Then repair it. Gate: (a) a new tests/test_boundary_flux_derivative.py, on one diverted and one limited fixture, over a batch of at least eight seeded directions, asserts that the boundary-flux JVP matches a central difference within a bound stated with its step, and that a no-selection control agrees to 1e-10; it fails at the dispatch base. (b) benchmarks/moment_map_derivative_contract.py, re-run at the committed revision with a SHA-256 of the driver source in the receipt, shows boundary_flux agreeing at the axis-flux level and names the next disagreeing stage, if any. A separate clip-quadrature custom_jvp defect is being repaired by session S22 in nova/equilibrium/clip_quadrature.py; do not edit that file, and expect the downstream support stages to stay off until both land. (c) test_the_moment_map_is_differentiable_against_finite_differences is reported with its value; do not widen any tolerance. (d) tests/test_equilibrium_forward_solve.py and every tests/test_*topology*.py file add no failure against the dispatch base, compared by test id. (e) Re-render stage-derivatives.png into this node's figures directory at the repository's data-ink sizes: 22 pt axis labels, 20 pt ticks and direct labels, and direct labels on the boundary-flux and axis-flux curves. Run long or GPU steps through RECKON_ALLOW_NESTED_LAUNCH=1 scripts/nova_lane/run.sh --rungs h200 --force-submit; the coordinator authorises this launch path, and the general fence does not forbid it. For a base tree, use git archive of the base revision restricted to nova tests benchmarks scripts, extracted under /tmp with PYTHONPATH pointing there, and remove it before writing the manifest, because .git/worktrees is read-only in this fence and /tmp on this node filled earlier tonight. Every uv command carries --no-sync and nothing runs uv sync. Write the manifest before any long step; its status is one of complete, blocked or failed.",
